<th id="S5.T5.4.1.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 5.0pt;">FP32</th>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 5.0pt;">92.74</td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.11.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 5.0pt;">83.38</td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.11.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 5.0pt;">90.65</td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.11.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 5.0pt;">77.10</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T5.4.1.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T5.4.1.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding:1pt 5.0pt;">Naïve</th>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 5.0pt;">35.12</td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 5.0pt;">26.38</td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.12.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 5.0pt;">30.55</td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.12.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 5.0pt;">20.92</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T5.4.1.13" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T5.4.1.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;padding:1pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.4.1.13.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">w/ RegCache</span></th>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;padding:1pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.4.1.13.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">82.59 <span id="S5.T5.4.1.13.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#009100;">(+47.47)</span></span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.13.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;padding:1pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.4.1.13.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">68.29 <span id="S5.T5.4.1.13.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#009100;">(+41.91)</span></span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.13.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;padding:1pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.4.1.13.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">81.83 <span id="S5.T5.4.1.13.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#009100;">(+51.28)</span></span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.1.13.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;padding:1pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.4.1.13.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">53.92 <span id="S5.T5.4.1.13.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#009100;">(+33.00)</span></span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Universality of prefixes.</span>
Since the prefix search procedure in RegCache involves validations on the training split of the ImageNet-1K dataset, we also assess whether the learned prefix remains effective on other datasets, as the register token might have overfitted to ImageNet-1K. The results in <a href="#S5.T5" title="In 5.2 Experimental results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Post-training quantization of vision encoders needs prefixing registers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> indicate that the prefix from ImageNet-1k remains effective on other datasets, suggesting that it acts as a universal register token.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation study.</span> In <a href="#S5.T6" title="In 5.2 Experimental results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Post-training quantization of vision encoders needs prefixing registers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we ablate the effect of our two stage methods—(1) prefix caching and (2) token deleting—with quantization performance. The results show that prefix caching suppresses the growth of outliers and improves performance, as token deletion further reduces their magnitude for additional gains. Still, outlier tokens can be safely removed only with prefix caching, as prefix tokens play a similar role to outlier tokens; without it, removing outliers in quantization-sensitive layers severely degrades performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T6" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:50%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span><span id="S5.T6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation studies.</span> We evaluate each component of RegCache on SigLIP.</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T6.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T6.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T6.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T6.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></th>
<th id="S5.T6.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T6.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">IN-1K acc.</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T6.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
